<title>USA: Orange County suits to be heard in district court.</title>
<headline>Orange County suits to be heard in district court.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA ANA, Calif. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. District Judge on Thursday ruled that the massive Orange County, Calif., lawsuits against Merrill Lynch &amp; Co and several other firms be removed from U.S. Bankruptcy Court, the county said.</p>
<p>U.S. District Judge Gary Taylor granted motions by Merrill Lynch, the Student Loan Marketing Association, KPMG Peat Marwick LLP, Rauscher Pierce Refsnes Inc and McGraw-Hill Cos Inc's Standard &amp; Poor's Corp to move the county's complaints from bankruptcy to federal district court, according to county attorneys.</p>
</text>
